From 30089106527045c7309617ef932a8435b33354a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:10:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/22] fix(ops): nginx edge hardening; db-init retries
 connection errors and compose failures show the migration log

B-21: the generated nginx config advertised its version, wrote an access
log with every chat URL and query string onto an unbounded tmpfs, used the
OpenSSL default TLS 1.2 cipher list and left session tickets on (no key
rotation -> weaker forward secrecy). Now server_tokens off, access_log off
(the app has its own redacted request log), Mozilla-intermediate TLS 1.2
suites, ssl_session_tickets off; the /var/log/nginx tmpfs is capped at 64m.

B-22: python -m app.migrate ran once; a connection refused through PgBouncer
in the first second after "healthy" failed the whole compose up with a bare
exit code. Each of the three migration steps now retries OperationalError/
DBAPIError/OSError up to 6 times (1,2,4,8,15 s) and exits with a clear
message; other errors are not retried. stack.sh's compose_up_or_explain
prints the last 60 lines of the db-init container when compose up fails.

Tests: tests/test_migrate_retry.py; nginx hardening assertions added to
tests/test_tls_certificate.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
